<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16571" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστοχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>missing the mark, aiming
				badly at,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					19e
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.370
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Tib.
			</span></i> Ill.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs.,
				<i>aiming amiss, random,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀστόχου διανοίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					587a9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηγορία</span>”
				<i>aimless, absurd,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.49.4
				</span></i>
			; of a person, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ind.Sto.</u>
				32
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-χως</span>”
				<i>amiss,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					116.14
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.74.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mort.</u>
				33
			</span></i>.</div>
